* 
* Sample_selection_moments.do
* 
* * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *
* Generates the target moments consumed by the Sample Selection notebook
* (Sample Selection Discrete.ipynb / sample_selection_spain.py): the 5-bin
* spell-completion share distribution of max_TC_sample, for four nested Spain
* time windows (2011-, 2005-, 1999-, 1992-), matching Germany's harmonised
* sample restrictions.
* 
* Trimmed 2026-07-21 from Descriptive_stats_other_lean_incidence.do, which is
* kept in full (unchanged) for reference and further checks. This file keeps
* only what Sample Selection actually reads: the "long" (5-bin: 0, .5, 1, 1.5,
* 2) keytab table for each window. Demographics, education, industry, and
* duration tables for the 2011 window are now generated by
* Descriptive_stats_main.do instead.
* 
* Output (one per window):
*   descriptive_stats/desstats_sple_keytab{2011,2005,1999,1992}_long.log
*     one-way tab of max_TC_sample (samesame==1, one row per individual)
* 
* Data: baseline_SE_21.dta
* * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *

clear

global end_year = 2021

use "baseline_SE_21.dta", clear

sort id jobcount dtin

* Samesame: identify individuals, one row per person
gen samesame = (id != id[_n+1])

* cause_next: needed for the glitch/retirement drop below
sort id jobcount dtin dtout
by id: gen cause_next = cause[_n+1]

* Keeping unfinished spells
drop if unfin == 1 & samesame == 0

* Time window: no spells after $end_year
drop if year_in > $end_year

global strict_cleaning = 1

* Saving data for the different time windows
tempfile base_data
save `base_data'

foreach yy in 2011 2005 1999 1992 {

use `base_data', clear

* Time window: no spells finishing before `yy'
drop if year_out < `yy'

* Type of worker restrictions (harmonised with Germany)
drop if ever_disc == 1 & $strict_cleaning > 0
drop if ever_fun  == 1 & $strict_cleaning > 0
drop if ever_se   == 1 & $strict_cleaning == 2
drop if share_total_a > 0.5 & $strict_cleaning == 1

* Drop if next spell was a glitch (or retirement)
drop if cause_next == 60
drop if cause == 58

* Counting number of completed unstable cycles
sort id state_c dtin dtout
by id state_c: gen n_TC_sample = _n if state_c == "TU"

* Correction for unfinished spells (don't count as completed)
gen unfinTC = (state_c == "TU" & unfin == 1)
replace n_TC_sample = n_TC_sample - 1 if unfinTC == 1

egen max_TC_sample = max(n_TC_sample), by(id)
replace max_TC_sample = 0 if max_TC_sample == .
replace max_TC_sample = 2 if max_TC_sample > 2

* 5-bin "long" definition: separate those with only an unfinished spell
egen OnlyOneUnfinTC  = max(unfinTC), by(id)
gen  OneAndOneUnfinTC = OnlyOneUnfinTC
replace OnlyOneUnfinTC   = 0 if max_TC_sample > 0
replace OneAndOneUnfinTC = 0 if max_TC_sample != 1
replace max_TC_sample = 0.5 if OnlyOneUnfinTC   == 1  // one unfinished unstable
replace max_TC_sample = 1.5 if OneAndOneUnfinTC == 1  // one finished + one unfinished

* Samesame: reset after the drops above
sort id dtin dtout
drop samesame
gen samesame = (id != id[_n+1])

log using "./descriptive_stats/desstats_sple_keytab`yy'_long.log", replace
tab max_TC_sample if samesame == 1
log close

}

clear
